# Anti-loss protocol — see CLAUDE.md §1, Cause 3.
#
# The Theme Editor rewrites these files server-side every time the merchant
# customises anything. Pushing our local copies over them destroys their work.
# They are pushed ONCE, on the very first deploy, and never again.
#
# FIRST DEPLOY ONLY: rename this file to .shopifyignore.off, push, rename back.
#   mv .shopifyignore .shopifyignore.off
#   shopify theme push --store getpawly.myshopify.com --theme <UNPUBLISHED_ID>
#   mv .shopifyignore.off .shopifyignore
#
# Every deploy after that: leave this file exactly as it is.

config/settings_data.json
templates/*.json

# Never ship editor noise
.DS_Store
*.map
